<Base title="Responsible disclosure" description="How to report a security issue in PHP Hub, and how we handle vulnerability information.">
<div class="page-prose"><h1>Responsible disclosure</h1>
<h2>Found a problem with this site?</h2><p>If you believe you've found a security issue in PHP Hub or its tools, please report it privately via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Include steps to reproduce. Please give us reasonable time to fix it before any public disclosure, and avoid accessing other people's data or disrupting the service.</p>
<h2>How we publish vulnerability information</h2>
<ul><li>We write about vulnerabilities only after a fix or official advisory is public.</li><li>We do not publish working exploit code.</li><li>Detection tips (such as log patterns) are shared to help defenders.</li></ul>
<h2>Found a bug in someone else's software?</h2><p>Report it to the vendor or maintainer first. For PHP itself, see php.net's security reporting process; for WordPress plugins, the plugin author or a coordinator such as Patchstack or Wordfence.</p></div></Base>
